## Manual Verification Strategy
Automated scanners generate massive, noisy log results that often lead to inaccurate findings. To successfully identify legitimate high-paying structural bugs, human validation of the HTTP server responses is strictly required. [15, 16, 17] 

* The [1Win HackerOne Testing Window](https://hackerone.com/1win_com/policy_versions): If you choose to manually evaluate these vulnerabilities on the live production environment, you must adhere strictly to the operational bounds defined by the platform policy. Automated testing tool limits must remain strictly below 5 concurrent requests per second to prevent platform disruption. [18] 



